{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/971320-an-open-letter-to-onyx-path-forums-and-the-white-wolf-fandom","id":971320,"title":"An Open Letter to Onyx Path Forums and the White Wolf Fandom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T08:03:21-07:00","id":971320,"title":"An Open Letter to Onyx Path Forums and the White Wolf Fandom","content":"Okay, this is technically about WoD and CofD, but since I'm discussing both and more importantly, the fans and community surrounding these games, I figured I'd post it here in the general board. I have some things I need to get off my chest and that need to be addressed.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to sugar-coat it, I'm widely disliked here and I know it. And I think I know why. It's because of two things. The first is that I have an unconventional approach to WoD and CofD games (I like the settings but not their themes or the metaplot in the case of oWoD) and more importantly, that I am very adamant about said unconventional approach (I genuinely prefer &quot;Dark Superheroes&quot; over &quot;Personal Horror&quot; and am not afraid to admit it), often to the point of obnoxiousness. And for that, I am truly sorry. Part of it came from the way I was treated back on the old White Wolf forums (some of you who know my old username will definitely remember) and part of it comes from bad LARP experiences in real life. Sort of a developed knee-jerk reaction to things.<br /> <br /> Often, people tell me that I should play &quot;Some Other Game&quot;, that WoD and CofD are not for me and that I'm &quot;playing the game wrong&quot;. One user even has the &quot;Some Other Game&quot; argument in her signature, no doubt partly inspired by me and my obnoxious and horrible behavior. Usually, I would get infuriated at the &quot;Some Other Game&quot; argument, saying that I didn't want &quot;Some Other Game&quot; but a modified WoD or CofD instead. But now I'm beginning to think they may be right. Maybe I should just give up on White Wolf and play &quot;Some Other Game&quot;.<br /> <br /> I know it's just a game and that I shouldn't be worrying this much about it. But given the fact that this game and my interactions with it and its fans has given me nothing but trouble and misery for the past few years, then maybe I should move on. Maybe I should just stick to BESM and the like and leave WoD for the serious gamers. It's obvious that I'm in the minority when it comes to my playstyle and how I like the WoD and CofD to be.<br /> <br /> In short, I am sorry for my awful behavior on these forums and I really want to like the WoD and CofD games, but maybe I should give up on them, at least for a little while. Should I continue to play and promote my modified WoD games or should I quit and play something else? What should I do?<br /> <br /> Any input would be appreciated and I'd like this thread to keep civil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:23:16-07:00","id":971329,"title":"","content":"You should play what you want to play- I knows nothing about any previous argument you had with people in those forums, but it is your game, your books and what makes you feel good. As long as no one tries to shove their preferred game-style into the other's throat, or expect the game to change specifically for you, what the problem could be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:27:32-07:00","id":971330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/971320-an-open-letter-to-onyx-path-forums-and-the-white-wolf-fandom#post971320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this is technically about WoD and CofD, but since I'm discussing both and more importantly, the fans and community surrounding these games, I figured I'd post it here in the general board. I have some things I need to get off my chest and that need to be addressed.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to sugar-coat it, I'm widely disliked here and I know it. And I think I know why. It's because of two things. The first is that I have an unconventional approach to WoD and CofD games (I like the settings but not their themes or the metaplot in the case of oWoD) and more importantly, that I am very adamant about said unconventional approach (I genuinely prefer &quot;Dark Superheroes&quot; over &quot;Personal Horror&quot; and am not afraid to admit it), often to the point of obnoxiousness. And for that, I am truly sorry. Part of it came from the way I was treated back on the old White Wolf forums (some of you who know my old username will definitely remember) and part of it comes from bad LARP experiences in real life. Sort of a developed knee-jerk reaction to things.<br /> <br /> Often, people tell me that I should play &quot;Some Other Game&quot;, that WoD and CofD are not for me and that I'm &quot;playing the game wrong&quot;. One user even has the &quot;Some Other Game&quot; argument in her signature, no doubt partly inspired by me and my obnoxious and horrible behavior. Usually, I would get infuriated at the &quot;Some Other Game&quot; argument, saying that I didn't want &quot;Some Other Game&quot; but a modified WoD or CofD instead. But now I'm beginning to think they may be right. Maybe I should just give up on White Wolf and play &quot;Some Other Game&quot;.<br /> <br /> I know it's just a game and that I shouldn't be worrying this much about it. But given the fact that this game and my interactions with it and its fans has given me nothing but trouble and misery for the past few years, then maybe I should move on. Maybe I should just stick to BESM and the like and leave WoD for the serious gamers. It's obvious that I'm in the minority when it comes to my playstyle and how I like the WoD and CofD to be.<br /> <br /> In short, I am sorry for my awful behavior on these forums and I really want to like the WoD and CofD games, but maybe I should give up on them, at least for a little while. Should I continue to play and promote my modified WoD games or should I quit and play something else? What should I do?<br /> <br /> Any input would be appreciated and I'd like this thread to keep civil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't consider myself a &quot;gamer&quot; at all. But that's really neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> I can't tell you what to play and what not to play. It's not my job and it's not my place. I think you should play whatever you want in whatever way you want with whatever mods you like. That's not the issue.<br /> <br /> What is an issue--to me, and I'm not a moderator--is treating the others on the forum like shit for playing the game in a different way, especially when you're the one making the mods. Now. To be completely honest with you, I don't especially recognize your username, so I'm taking your word for it that you've been treating people on the forum like shit. I'm not going to look through your posting history because even if you haven't been respectful here to this point, it sounds like you're ready to make amends, and I don't want to prejudice my reception of you by introducing bad behavior. So I have a few thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) I think most of us are willing to meet you halfway if you fix your behavior (which I'm assuming has been bad because you're saying it has).<br /> 2) Let's just say that you decide the forums are not a safe place for you to post and participate anymore (which I hope you don't). That shouldn't have any bearing on whether or not you continue playing the game your way.<br /> <br /> And that's all for now, but I may edit as more thoughts come.<br /> <br /> Again, I have no recollection of your bad behavior, and I'm not going to look for those posts. So, at least with me, you have someone willing to give you a second (first?) chance, if you put in the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:07:18-07:00","id":971345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/971320-an-open-letter-to-onyx-path-forums-and-the-white-wolf-fandom?p=971330#post971330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't consider myself a &quot;gamer&quot; at all. But that's really neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> I can't tell you what to play and what not to play. It's not my job and it's not my place. I think you should play whatever you want in whatever way you want with whatever mods you like. That's not the issue.<br /> <br /> What is an issue--to me, and I'm not a moderator--is treating the others on the forum like shit for playing the game in a different way, especially when you're the one making the mods. Now. To be completely honest with you, I don't especially recognize your username, so I'm taking your word for it that you've been treating people on the forum like shit. I'm not going to look through your posting history because even if you haven't been respectful here to this point, it sounds like you're ready to make amends, and I don't want to prejudice my reception of you by introducing bad behavior. So I have a few thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) I think most of us are willing to meet you halfway if you fix your behavior (which I'm assuming has been bad because you're saying it has).<br /> 2) Let's just say that you decide the forums are not a safe place for you to post and participate anymore (which I hope you don't). That shouldn't have any bearing on whether or not you continue playing the game your way.<br /> <br /> And that's all for now, but I may edit as more thoughts come.<br /> <br /> Again, I have no recollection of your bad behavior, and I'm not going to look for those posts. So, at least with me, you have someone willing to give you a second (first?) chance, if you put in the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThen I will improve my behavior and continue to work on things better. It's not so much that I treat people like shit but rather that I'm defensive and always argue with people, and I want to stop doing that. I'm sick of arguing, I want things to be better.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should take a week or two off just to clear my head. I've been feeling guilty about my past and sadly have been wallowing in bad memories, which is never a good thing to do. The past is just that, the past. I should focus on the present and look forward to the future.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:51:11-07:00","id":971366,"title":"","content":"I haven't interacted with you much in the WoD forums (I don't often visit the WoD forums), so I don't know if anything particularly contentious has happened with you there lately, but at least on the CofD forums, you've been perfectly civil lately. And no one has flagged any of your posts recently, so this might be a case of you being unduly hard on yourself. Granted, in the past you've been very vocally insistent about your preferences, but that hasn't caused any issues as far as I remember for the last few years.<br /> <br /> At any rate, it's perfectly fine to enjoy these games any way you want. If you like the settings and the rules but don't like the themes or the metaplot, there is nothing at all wrong with hacking them to better suit your preferences. A lot of people do so and get along just fine with the other users on these forums. It only becomes a problem when people harp on about how much they hate XYZ about a game and how it totally ruins it for them. That grates on people who do like XYZ and leaves everyone wondering why they're here if they hate the game so much. That's really what Atamajaki's signature is referring to. If you love playing your hacked and homebrewed version of the game, that's great! More power to you. If, however, the very premise of the game grinds your gears so much that you feel the need to come to the forums for the game and rant about how awful it is, you might be better off not playing it. You've always struck me as the former.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am sorry if anything I've said has pushed you to this point, and hope the community doesn't make you feel unwelcome to the point of quitting the game. What ever you decide to do, don't let other people tell you what you can or can't enjoy. Play the games you like in the way you like to play them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:35:41-07:00","id":971389,"title":"","content":"Go forth and be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:50:10-07:00","id":971434,"title":"","content":"As others have noted, there is a very wide substantive and psychological gulf between threads concerning discussions about how someone prefers to alter the setting or include house rules in their personal games and other threads incessantly complaining about the setting and themes and demanding obviously radical changes to suit personal tastes, despite the fact that the clear majority of everyone else (the actual intended audience), more or less, likes things just the way they are.<br /> <br /> The former is part and parcel of expected forum discussion, the latter ranges form immature whining to trollish, disruptive behavior.<br /> <br /> As to why others might suggest you explore other games, it's not really that surprising. The very foundation of the CofD is it's designed and intended as a modern horror setting. If you want &quot;dark superhero,&quot; science fiction, steampunk, transhuman, fantasy, or any other of a myriad of other RPG genres, there are ample offerings. Demanding that the CofD essentially alter its basic premises to suit you will not lead to productive discussions and implicitly devalues (and depending on style, often very strongly insults) those who like the genre and setting as presented and intended as well as the creative vision, professionalism and material of the developers and writers on the various game lines.<br /> <br /> Simply, its quite easy to amicably discuss the changes you like or would make in the setting (or seek help to make such changes) without doing little more than offering shrill and repeated criticisms of the setting and those who enjoy it. If you or anyone else cannot thread that proverbial needle, pushback is to be expected, and will likely not be kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:17:06-07:00","id":971448,"title":"","content":"FWIW Camilla, I don't hate you, and my signature has everything to do with the incessant Promethean debates more than anything to with you. There's nothing wrong with hacking the themes of a game until you start going after the fans and writers for enjoying the default, which is where there's been friction with you in the past. Nobody really cares what you change at your table; it only gets heated when everyone else gets called wrong.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm a little confused by the desire to so radically alter the WoD and CofD instead of going after something else. If you want urban fantasy with monsters, the Dresden Files RPG looks great and the upcoming new edition of Scion might cover that with a little less stress. If urban fantasy with heavy drama and politics is your thing, Urban Shadows is fucking incredible, and id you want actual superheroes take a look at Better Angels, the game of normal people given demonic superpowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:29:24-07:00","id":971458,"title":"","content":"Dude...play what makes you happy. Don't look for the satisfaction of others on these forums. Look for the satisfaction of yourself. I don't see eye to eye with probably 70% of the forum users here, and I'd say it's around 100% over at rpg.net. I've also noticed an increasing distance philosophically between myself and Onyx Path writers--especially as I grow older. <br /> <br /> Who cares? Play what makes you happy. That's what matters.<br /> <br /> I remember being called all sorts of insults for suggesting I would like to play a Black Spiral Dancers game. Until I ventured forth and found others who felt exactly the same way that I did. And guess what? We had an AWESOME time(even though it was only a 4 session game). <br /> <br /> If the future plans of White Wolf and/or Onyx Path doesn't jive with you(like myself), there's always the old games/books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:31:40-07:00","id":971462,"title":"","content":"The only beef I have with you is your tendency to perpetually paint all of the WoD games with Vampire's personal horror brush. The other games don't really share its focus for/obsession with that theme. Perhaps that's just a difference in two personal focuses on games shooting past each other, though; I'm mainly with Werewolf, and my reaction to &quot;why are you so focused on personal horror&quot; is to blink and ask &quot;wait what?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:37:52-07:00","id":971465,"title":"","content":"I've never seen you doing anything objectionable, and at the very least I've probably been more of an ass on the forums recently. <br /> <br /> I don't think what you're looking for really deviates that far from some of the canons. Awakening, for example, is pretty much completely a dark occult superhero game, and if you're looking for that, you should check it out. If you want more over the top monster action, oWoD downplays the personal in favor of gonzo splatterpunk. <br /> <br /> And I'm not going to tell you to &quot;play something else&quot; in this case, because what you're asking for isn't that radical. Plus, there are other reasons. None of those other games have all the support and material and community that ChroD has. I, personally, do not want to support the Dresden Files franchise. And so on. As an example, just because I love Unknown Armies doesn't mean that I don't sometimes want to play a self-destructive postmodern sorcerer in ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:50:26-07:00","id":971471,"title":"","content":"Maybe I am being too hard on myself. It's been rough for me these past few weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:52:36-07:00","id":971475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/971320-an-open-letter-to-onyx-path-forums-and-the-white-wolf-fandom?p=971462#post971462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Perhaps that's just a difference in two personal focuses on games shooting past each other, though; I'm mainly with Werewolf, and my reaction to &amp;quot;why are you so focused on personal horror&amp;quot; is to blink and ask &amp;quot;wait what?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... Weird, personal horror is a big part of my Werewolf games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:23:37-07:00","id":971492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/971320-an-open-letter-to-onyx-path-forums-and-the-white-wolf-fandom?p=971465#post971465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakening, for example, is pretty much completely a dark occult superhero game,</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really not. I mean, you can play it that way, just as you can play vampire as blood-powered superheroes. But it's not the default assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}